  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed change of use would result in the loss of an existing retail premises within a Local Centre, which would be inconsistent with the primary retail function of the local centre and disrupting the continuity of the retail frontage, contrary to Polices CP13 and CP17 within the Core Strategy and Policy DMD 28 within the Development Management Document.",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its insufficient provision of private amenity space, insufficient ceiling heights, lack of natural light /daylight would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD8, DMD9 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, would contribute unacceptably to parking congestion in the surrounding area which would give rise to conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of vehicular traffic and pedestrians, and fail to encourage sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies T4, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of adequate cycle parking would fail to provide a secure, convenient and high quality facility for all types of bicycles and would fail to promote or prioritise the use of sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies T5 of the London Plan (2021), CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of adequate waste storage would fail to provide a convenient and accessible facility for managing waste generated by the development for future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies T7 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP22 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) Policy DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Enfield Household Waste and Recycling Guidance for New Developments (2024)."
  ],
